<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n22772" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">indĭcātĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>an indicating</i>, <i>setting</i>, or <i>rating</i> the valuation of a thing, <i>a valuation;</i> hence, <i>value</i>,
				<i>price</i>, <i>rate</i> (mostly
			ante- and post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tua merx est, tua indicatio est,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Pers. 4, 4, 37</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mellis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					22, 24, 50, § 109</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">temeraria,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig. 19, 1, 13, § 3</span></i>
			.</div>
